    "_comment": "Concurrency is measured at a generation-heavy tier as well as a short one. At 'short' (128 output tokens) a ~700 ms per-request prefill dominates wall time and prefill is per-row serial by design, so aggregate throughput mostly measures ADMISSION LATENCY, not batched decode. 'longgen' (1k output) is where continuous batching can actually show its value. Measured 2026-08-21: gpt-oss-20b TTFT went 727/1614/3122/5883 ms for c1/c2/c4/c8 \u2014 linear in N \u2014 while per-request decode fell only 4.3x over an 8x concurrency increase."
  }
